{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared fixtures for the editing contract. Read by BOTH the TypeScript",
    "suite in this repo and the Python suite in the dreamlake SDK, so the two",
    "implementations of one rule are checked against the same data rather than",
    "against each other's prose.",
    "",
    "`op` is the operation, `args` its arguments, and either `out` (expected",
    "document) or `error` (the class of refusal). Documents are written with",
    "real newlines via \\n so both languages read them identically.",
    "",
    "When this file changes, both suites change with it. That is the point:",
    "there is one place to state what an edit means."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "replace-one-match",
      "doc": "# Title\n\nDraft one\n",
      "op": "replace",
      "args": {
        "text": "Published",
        "query": "Draft"
      },
      "out": "# Title\n\nPublished one\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "replace-ambiguous-is-refused",
      "doc": "Draft one\nDraft two\n",
      "op": "replace",
      "args": {
        "text": "X",
        "query": "Draft"
      },
      "error": "AmbiguousMatch"
    },
    {
      "name": "replace-all",
      "doc": "Draft one\nDraft two\n",
      "op": "replace",
      "args": {
        "text": "Published",
        "query": "Draft",
        "all": true
      },
      "out": "Published one\nPublished two\n"
    },
